<title>CANADA: CANADA MAY RETAIL SALES RISE 0.5 PCT.</title>
<headline>CANADA MAY RETAIL SALES RISE 0.5 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian retail sales rose 0.5 percent in May to a seasonally adjusted C$19.25 billion from a revised C$19.16 billion (C$18.88 billion) in April, Statistics Canada said on Monday.</p>
<p>				    Month pct    Year pct    Total</p>
<p>Sales, seasonally adjusted     +0.5	 +7.6     C$19.25 bln</p>
<p>Sales, ex vehicles, s/a	  -0.1	 +5.2     C$14.36 bln</p>
<p>Sales, unadjusted		  n/a	  +8.6     C$21.20 bln</p>
<p>Statistics Canada said early indications for June sales were for an increase in the number of new motor vehicles sold. The number of employees in retail trade rose by 0.2 percent in</p>
